# expanded-cinema

Daily Three.js sketch agent project (system-level handoff kept outside this repo).

## Decisions

- **Workspace shape**: modeled on [ts-cli-template](https://github.com/joelhooks/ts-cli-template)
— pnpm workspaces (`apps/*`, `packages/*`) + Turborepo, strict TS 7.0.2,
  oxlint/ultracite + oxfmt, devEngines pinning Node >=24.18 / pnpm 11.3.0.
- **Rendering**: WebGPU (three.js `WebGPURenderer`), not WebGL. Fallback story:
  report rather than silently substitute.
- **Effect**: effect 3.22.2 as the runtime backbone — video sources, WebGPU
  device acquisition, and any node-side pipeline steps are Effects, not
  untyped promises.
- **XState v6 alpha**: `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.53` pinned exactly (alpha, no caret)
  for the sketch/run lifecycle machine. API verified from the vendored mirror
  (`setup`, `createMachine`, `createActor`, `fromPromise`, `fromCallback`,
  `assign` all present in `packages/core/src`).
- **Video sources**: real video files are the projection material. `videos/`
  at workspace root holds source clips; `scripts/catalog-videos.mjs` will
  generate `apps/sketch/catalog.json` (file + sha256). Classification:
  `*.mp4` direct-play, `*.readback.mp4` gpu-readback study input,
  `*.orchestration.mp4` suppressed from the loop. Starter placeholder:
  `apps/sketch/public/videos/starter.mp4`.
- **Cloud infra**: alchemy (`2.0.0-beta.77`) for Cloudflare. Publishing target
  is **cinema.wzrrd.sh** via the `wzrrd.sh` zone (pattern proven in a local stack file:
  custom-domain Workers routes beat
  the zone's wildcard because Routes beat custom domains; stage-suffixed
  hostnames for previews). Reference examples vendored: the alchemy repo's
  `examples/cloudflare-website-vite` (SPA on Workers w/ `Website.Vite`) and
  another local example (prebuilt worker + `assets.directory`).
- **Public repo**: GitHub via `gh`, public. ShitRat actor rule does not
  apply here (manual, Joel-approved publish; no app access needed).
- **Vendored source mirrors** (`.agent_sources/github.com/`, via
  `scripts/vendor-agent-sources.sh`, reference-only):
  `mrdoob/three` @ r186, `Effect-TS/effect`, `statelyai/xstate`,
  `alchemy-run/alchemy` @ 1eccc046.
- **State layers** (per system handoff): `state/ledger.jsonl` canonical for
  run outcomes; `STATE.json`, `STUDIES.md`, `LOG.md` derived pointers;
  this Brain is for durable decisions/terms, not run history.
- **Scheduling & delivery**: `joelclaw wake` for cadence, `joelclaw notify
  send` for daily report, wzrrd for review links. No run has been fired.
- **VISION.md** (2026-09-13): repo-scoped, external audience (gallery
  viewers, contributors). Captures the body-of-work intent ("bounce around
  within similar topics", not linear, not random), the sign-off list (model
  pin, backend, major deps, publishing, spend, scheduling, brief edits, asset
  licensing, canonical studies), and the will-not-do list (forever loop,
  multi-agent, WebGL target, public run history, second ledger). `AGENTS.md`
  points at it for intent only; operational rules stay in `AGENTS.md`.
  Hosting wording follows the code (alchemy → Workers), not the older
  handoff's Pages + wrangler wording.
- **Live gallery via MCP** (Joel, 2026-09-13, verbatim: "the page needs to
  refresh itself dynamically, so we should be able to use mcp to modify the
  site live and occasionally push when updates are needed"). The gallery
  reads content from a runtime store; an authenticated MCP tool writes to it;
  an open page picks up changes without a rebuild. Git push + deploy is a
  code checkpoint, not the per-study delivery path. The MCP write surface is
  a publishing capability on a public site: auth and allowed operations need
  Joel's sign-off. Implementation (KV/R2 manifest vs Durable Object,
  polling vs SSE/WebSocket) is undecided.

## Open questions

- **Effect version drift**: `apps/sketch` declares `effect@3.22.2` and the
  README says Effect 3.22, but the workspace `overrides` in
  `pnpm-workspace.yaml` force `effect@4.0.0-rc.112` everywhere, and that is
  what is installed under `apps/sketch/node_modules`. Either the sketch app
  is really on v4 rc and docs should say so, or the override should be scoped
  to `packages/infra`. Decide before the pipeline code leans on either API.

- Near-term: an actual R2 bucket wiring for previews/clips (alchemy
  `Cloudflare.Bucket`) — deferred until a real run produces artifacts.
- Whether the public site carries the gallery alone or also a run history
  page (default: gallery only).
